---
name: ui-theme
description: "Inspect, preview, install, activate, restore or remove a specified Studio, generated-design or OMP host theme. Use for explicit theme work with reversible ownership and capability checks."
---

# Manage the specified theme

Implementation target: activate with compatible Studio and host commands.

## Inputs and scope

Identify the requested operation and scope: dashboard appearance, generated product tokens, or OMP host theme. Resolve current theme, desired theme, ownership receipt, relevant artifact versions and host capabilities. A colour preference alone does not authorize host replacement.

## Workflow

Read the theme section of `.prism-rebuild/docs/PRODUCT-AND-UX.md` and relevant accessibility checks. Preview changes and verify semantic tokens, contrast, focus, state distinctions and reduced motion.

For generated design tokens, create a versioned design change with dependency impact and design-budget admission when paid work is needed. Dashboard preference changes do not rewrite approved artifacts.

For host installation, stage validated files, detect conflicts, preserve originals and record ownership. Verify activation through the actual host; a copied file is insufficient. Restore/uninstall only unchanged receipt-owned additions. Keep unrelated settings and user-modified files intact; report conflicts with a recovery path.

## Mode, outputs and exit

Guided obtains any relevant material design choice; YOLO may choose within existing scope. Both honour installation authority and budget. Use the installed host's supported operations; do not invent syntax or claim unavailable capabilities.

Return preview/result, scope, versions, validation and install/activation/restore receipts as applicable. Exit when the requested operation is verified or its exact blocker is recorded. Never claim a theme is active solely because template files were produced.
